Data Types, Literals & Variables
​The Materials Catalogue (Python Data Types)
​INT · BAR STOCK  
​Description: Whole numbers, exact and countable. Parts produced, stations on a line, teeth on a gear.  
​Examples: 42, 0, -3 \rightarrow says <class 'int'>.  
​FLOAT · GROUND FINISH  
​Description: Measured quantities with a decimal point. Diameters, temperatures, cycle times. The point is the certificate — 25.0 is float even though it looks whole.  
​Examples: 25.0, 0.05, 3.14 \rightarrow <class 'float'>.  
​STR · NAMEPLATE  
​Description: Text in quotes — engravings, labels, part numbers. Anything quoted is a nameplate, even if it looks like a number.  
​Examples: "VSSUT", "25", 'GO' \rightarrow <class 'str'>.  
​BOOL · LIMIT SWITCH  
​Description: Exactly two states: True or False. Capital first letter, no quotes. Every if/else you'll ever write runs on these.  
​Examples: True, False \rightarrow <class 'bool'>.  
​The Spectrometer: When in doubt, don't argue — measure. print(type(x)) settles every certification dispute in one line. Engineers verify; they don't guess.
  
